{"proposals":[],"assessments":[{"claim":"H150","status":"unresolved","investigation":"active","evidence":[]}],"narrative":"No assessments are due and no new independent validation requests remain. I activate H150 and request the 12 highest-value discovery analyses from the active pool. The priority is technical-validity robustness for the six accepted large/intermediate dependency axes under low Cas9 activity (cas9_activity_pct <= 67.7): H171 SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, H172 MSI-high/WRN, H173 TP53 wild-type/USP7, H174 CDKN2A loss/MDM2, H175 PTEN loss/STAT3, and H176 KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2. H176 is direction +1, so a positive signed estimate again means weaker NFE2L2 dependency with KEAP1 loss, consistent with the accepted reversal. For direction -1 hypotheses, positive signed estimates mean exposed has a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency, than comparator. These estimates must not be multiplied by direction again.

I also request robustness of accepted axes in important contexts: H150 tests CDKN2A loss/MDM2 dependency in high aneuploidy, completing copy-number instability robustness for the CDKN2A-MDM2 axis; H180 tests CDKN2A loss/MDM2 in batch_a; H181 tests SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 in high aneuploidy; and H182 tests TP53 wild-type/USP7 in high aneuploidy. If these remain near prior magnitudes with intervals excluding null, the dataset-level associations are less likely to be driven by low Cas9 quality, batch, or high aneuploidy confounding. If they attenuate or include null, acceptance should be restricted to adequate Cas9 or relevant contexts.

H179 asks whether BRAF-mutant cells show stronger BRAF dependency in the mechanistically cleaner KRAS-wild-type context; the prior overall BRAF-mutation contrast was near null. H178 is a broad exploratory STAT3 test, asking whether MSI-high cells have stronger STAT3 dependency than MSI-stable cells. Practical interpretation will use about 0.10 dependency-score units with interval excluding null for meaningful acceptance; very large effects around 0.8 are clearly important within this dataset, whereas near-null effects around 0.01-0.03 are not. Positive estimates with intervals including null will remain unresolved unless supported by context and size. These remain associations among measured variables, not causal or external generalizability claims.","research_notes":"Iteration 12 analyze. Activated H150 and ran 12 discovery comparisons. Low-Cas9 technical robustness: H171-H176 for SMARCA2, WRN, USP7, MDM2, STAT3, NFE2L2. Accepted-axis context robustness: H150 high-aneuploidy CDKN2A-MDM2, H180 batch_a CDKN2A-MDM2, H181 high-aneuploidy SMARCA4-SMARCA2, H182 high-aneuploidy TP53-USP7. Exploratory/context tests: H179 BRAF-mutant dependency in KRAS-WT, H178 MSI-high STAT3 dependency. Interpret exactly as signed; do not multiply by direction. Practical threshold ~0.10 with CI excluding zero; large ~0.8 robust; near-null 0.01-0.03 reject/not accept. No validation capacity remains.","run_analyses":["H171","H172","H173","H174","H175","H176","H150","H178","H179","H180","H181","H182"]}
